---
const faqs = [
  { q: "What is EcoRouter?", a: "A shared USDC spending account on Stellar for a team and its AI agents. The owner funds one account, and every person or agent pays from it under its own policy: an allowance per period, a cap per payment, a maximum number of payments, an expiry date and a list of approved services. A Soroban contract holds the money and enforces the policy." },
  { q: "Can I use real money?", a: "Not yet. EcoRouter runs on Stellar testnet only and the contracts have not been audited. Use test funds." },
  { q: "Can an assistant spend without limits?", a: "No. The assistant only proposes a payment. Code reads the amount from your sentence, the assistant can only pick a service from the spender's approved list, its output has no address field, and the contract then runs the full policy. Any of those stages can refuse, and the contract has the final say." },
  { q: "What happens when a payment is blocked?", a: "If it breaks a limit such as the cap or the allowance, it is held, not failed, and nothing moves. A person can ask for approval, and the owner sees the rule that caught it and how far over it was. Approving and paying are separate steps, and the payment refuses to settle if the service's payee changed in between. Payments from a paused spender, or to an unknown or suspended service, are refused outright." },
  { q: "Do I need a wallet?", a: "Yes, a Freighter wallet on Testnet. The team account and service registry are already deployed, and the app reads their addresses from the repo." },
  { q: "Can my team add an AI agent?", a: "Yes. Each agent is a spender with its own Stellar key and its own policy. It can pay on a schedule, for example $5 every day to a data API, or top up a service. When an agent's payment breaks a rule it stops there and does not become an approval request." },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="bg-[#FCFCF9]">
  <div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-5 py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] gap-10">
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <div class="eyebrow">06 · FAQ</div>
        <h2 class="text-[40px] sm:text-[48px] leading-[1.05] font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-ink">Questions</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white card divide-y divide-line overflow-hidden">
        {faqs.map((item) => (
          <details class="group px-5 sm:px-6">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none select-none py-5 text-[15px] font-medium text-ink gap-4">
              <span class="leading-snug">{item.q}</span>
              <span class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-surface-muted text-ink flex items-center justify-center transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14" /></svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <p class="pb-5 -mt-1 text-sm text-ink-secondary leading-relaxed pr-8">{item.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
